Bug 2056063 - Fix spurious "Running Filters" prompt after running filters on newsgroups. r=tobyp

Bug 2049194 moved gRunningFilters state management out of the global
meteor message handler and into runSelectedFilters(), so the flag is
now always set when filters run. However the only mechanism to clear
it was the "stop-meteors" handler, which depends on URL lifecycle
events from nsMsgMailNewsUrl::SetUrlState(). For newsgroup/offline
filter execution, nsMsgSearchSession uses SearchWOUrls() which never
creates URLs, so no "stop-meteors" is ever sent and gRunningFilters
stays true permanently.

Fix this by passing an nsIMsgOperationListener callback to
applyFiltersToFolders(). The filter executor calls OnStopOperation()
from OnEndExecution() when ALL filter processing is truly complete,
regardless of whether URLs were involved.

If the window is still open when the callback fires, also clean up
any leftover progress bar and status text as a failsafe against stray
meteor messages (to be removed when bug 2002774 lands).

Also fix the "Run Now" button being enabled while the folder picker
still shows "Choose folder…". The button was unconditionally enabled
in setFilterFolder() before a target folder was actually selected.
Move the enable logic entirely into updateButtons() where it is gated
on three conditions: filters are selected, a run folder is set, and
the server supports after-the-fact filtering. Store the last condition
in a gCanFilterAfterTheFact global so updateButtons() can read it
independently of the mutable disabled state. In the OnStopOperation
callback, call updateButtons() to re-evaluate all enable conditions
rather than unconditionally re-enabling the button — this handles
state changes that may have occurred during filter execution.

When selectFolder() returns false (folder not found in the menu),
clear _folder so the button stays disabled and the picker consistently
shows "Choose folder…". Also ensure updateButtons() runs after the
last filter is deleted by adding a clearSelection + updateButtons path.

Add browser test covering the button enable/disable lifecycle:
disabled on open → enabled after creating a filter → disabled after
deleting the last filter, tested against a newsgroup server.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313257


